WEBVTT

00:26.630 --> 00:32.550
Since being alone was tough, the two of us held hands.

00:33.050 --> 00:39.050
The two of us two were lonely, so we all stood in a circle and joined hands.

00:39.010 --> 00:47.270
I'm sure that's where we will gather our strength.

00:47.190 --> 00:52.230
Enough to stand up to any dream.

00:52.110 --> 00:54.860
Fly high towards the sky,

00:54.530 --> 00:59.030
Kick off the ground and send your voice to the heavens,

00:58.740 --> 01:04.080
Until you overcome those painful days.

01:03.870 --> 01:09.210
I'll never forget your voice, and I'll never forget your tears.

01:05.830 --> 01:05.870
The First Annual Make Kyousuke Chuckle Championships

01:08.830 --> 01:16.170
The future that we call "hope" begins now.

01:15.920 --> 01:26.980
Your feet will continue to step onward, even when the time of grief comes.

01:40.930 --> 01:43.970
How much further will this labyrinth extend?

01:44.770 --> 01:48.190
What kind of treasure is waiting for us at the end?

01:48.940 --> 01:53.980
And who exactly is Saya-san, who claims to be a spy?

01:54.480 --> 01:57.360
Everything was still a mystery to me.

01:58.860 --> 02:06.410
But even then I felt that the time I spent with this girl was precious to me.

02:07.370 --> 02:10.420
We've met before, haven't we?

02:18.670 --> 02:20.930
Why are you crying?

02:20.930 --> 02:23.220
I'm not crying...

02:24.470 --> 02:27.810
<i>That I had loved Saya-san...</i>

02:29.940 --> 02:31.350
<i>since long ago.</i>

02:33.730 --> 02:34.980
When exactly...

02:36.110 --> 02:38.860
did I fall in love with her?

02:40.780 --> 02:42.530
Next up is the fifth floor.

02:42.780 --> 02:44.870
There should be a stair—

02:44.870 --> 02:47.370
W-What are you staring at?!

02:47.370 --> 02:48.750
N-Nothing...

02:52.710 --> 02:55.750
We could be attacked at any moment...

02:55.750 --> 02:58.880
Yet you don't seem to have a care in the world.

02:59.130 --> 03:01.380
This is why taking along an amateur is so troublesome.

03:01.380 --> 03:04.430
Don't think you'll be able to find the treasure like—

03:14.270 --> 03:15.730
That was your fault!

03:15.730 --> 03:17.570
It's because you were staring at me!

03:17.900 --> 03:19.110
Now, now.

03:20.110 --> 03:21.280
Look at that.

03:26.450 --> 03:29.870
An entrance will probably open up if you pull on it.

03:30.540 --> 03:32.790
But I don't think we can reach it.

03:32.790 --> 03:33.920
Lend me your shoulder.

03:33.920 --> 03:34.500
Eh?

03:34.830 --> 03:36.590
I'm going to climb on top.

03:36.590 --> 03:38.040
Isn't that obvious?

03:45.050 --> 03:46.760
Go ahead.

03:46.970 --> 03:48.180
Sorry about this.

03:51.560 --> 03:53.310
All right, go ahead and stand up.

03:53.600 --> 03:54.560
Okay.

03:55.230 --> 03:56.480
Keep going.

03:59.770 --> 04:01.400
Just a little further.

04:02.150 --> 04:03.450
Riki-kun.

04:03.450 --> 04:04.490
I'm going to jump.

04:04.990 --> 04:06.410
Eh? Jump?

04:06.820 --> 04:08.030
Here I go!

04:17.380 --> 04:19.090
All right!

04:26.550 --> 04:27.640
Let's go.

04:27.720 --> 04:28.640
Yeah.

04:40.480 --> 04:42.150
W-What's that?

04:42.530 --> 04:44.650
It's just a stone statue.

04:55.960 --> 04:57.080
It's moving!

05:00.540 --> 05:02.250
A one-on-one battle.

05:02.250 --> 05:04.210
This must be a test of strength.

05:04.800 --> 05:05.970
We have to fight against <i>that</i>?

05:05.970 --> 05:08.680
We have to defeat this thing before we can move forward.

05:09.260 --> 05:11.220
I'll need you to think of a strategy.

05:11.220 --> 05:13.520
There should be a key to stopping him.

05:13.520 --> 05:14.720
What about you?

05:14.720 --> 05:17.350
Who's going to fight it if I don't?

05:17.350 --> 05:19.440
No way! It's too dangerous!

05:19.900 --> 05:21.480
I'm no amateur.

05:21.480 --> 05:23.650
I can take this thing on easily.

05:23.650 --> 05:25.650
You'll just get in my way, so step aside!

05:33.740 --> 05:35.290
Take this, you bastard!

05:58.480 --> 06:00.190
Hey! Look over here!

06:00.190 --> 06:01.770
I'll be your opponent!

06:07.110 --> 06:09.030
What's he trying to do?

06:41.440 --> 06:42.730
This is...

06:42.730 --> 06:44.810
Riki-kun, throw me your sword!

06:45.480 --> 06:45.940
What?

06:45.940 --> 06:47.400
Just throw it to me!

06:47.400 --> 06:48.940
Um, but..?

06:48.940 --> 06:50.530
Throw it before I get pissed!

06:50.700 --> 06:53.110
You gloomy scumbag!

07:13.180 --> 07:13.800
Saya!

07:22.640 --> 07:24.350
Did you hurt your leg?

07:24.350 --> 07:25.940
Seems like it.

07:28.570 --> 07:29.440
Wh—

07:30.320 --> 07:31.780
What are you doing?!

07:32.070 --> 07:35.780
It would be a problem if those guys were to show up at a time like this.

07:35.780 --> 07:37.620
L-L-Let me down!

07:37.620 --> 07:38.580
I can stand on my own!

07:38.580 --> 07:39.240
So heavy.

07:39.240 --> 07:44.250
Don't you know it's rude to call a lady heavy?!

07:46.460 --> 07:48.090
How pathetic...

07:48.090 --> 07:51.630
A professional spy having to rely on an amateur...

07:51.970 --> 07:53.090
It's humiliating.

07:53.090 --> 07:54.550
Go ahead and laugh.

07:54.800 --> 07:56.430
Come on, start laughing!

07:58.930 --> 08:00.060
Please don't move.

08:04.520 --> 08:05.980
Is this where you got hurt?

08:07.520 --> 08:08.770
You touched my foot!

08:08.770 --> 08:10.690
Are you going to take responsibility?!

08:10.690 --> 08:12.360
I'm a virgin, you know!

08:12.610 --> 08:16.490
Once you lay hands on a virgin, you have to take responsibility!

08:16.490 --> 08:19.450
That's a pretty dangerous statement...

08:19.450 --> 08:22.200
But I don't think it's broken.

08:22.200 --> 08:23.660
Thank goodness.

08:23.660 --> 08:27.790
Jeez, being around you really makes me lose my composure.

08:27.790 --> 08:30.090
It's that damn smile of yours.

08:31.840 --> 08:34.970
Also... don't lie to me...

08:35.840 --> 08:38.850
But back then, during that fight...

08:39.390 --> 08:40.850
You called me...

08:41.930 --> 08:43.730
Saya, didn't you?

08:44.430 --> 08:45.140
Yeah.

08:45.140 --> 08:46.270
I did.

08:47.520 --> 08:49.730
Saya-san is fine as it is...

08:49.730 --> 08:52.940
Don't you think "Saya" is being a little too over-familiar?

08:52.940 --> 08:54.990
I wanted to try calling you that way.

08:56.490 --> 08:57.820
"Saya."

08:58.950 --> 09:00.200
I don't know when...

09:00.700 --> 09:04.330
but I feel like I used to call you that a long time ago.

09:08.460 --> 09:12.130
U-Um, Riki-kun...

09:13.920 --> 09:14.550
Yes?

09:16.420 --> 09:18.550
I'm going to tell you something important.

09:19.010 --> 09:20.890
So please don't act surprised.

09:22.930 --> 09:23.810
I...

09:24.680 --> 09:26.810
I like you.

09:29.900 --> 09:33.730
And sometimes on the battlefield people usually...

09:34.360 --> 09:37.530
do stuff like this, sooo...

09:40.660 --> 09:41.990
Y-You know...

09:41.990 --> 09:42.660
Eh?

09:42.660 --> 09:45.580
I feel like I was hurt really badly just now...

09:45.830 --> 09:49.790
And because of that, I'm suddenly getting this strong urge to kill you slowly...

09:50.330 --> 09:51.330
Can I kill you?

09:51.330 --> 09:52.000
What?!

09:52.000 --> 09:53.500
Like hell you can!

09:53.500 --> 09:54.840
Then I'll just drop dead!

09:54.840 --> 09:56.670
W-Why would you have to—

09:57.840 --> 09:58.630
Because...

09:58.840 --> 10:00.510
Because, because, because!

10:01.340 --> 10:02.100
Because!

10:02.100 --> 10:05.390
Because you avoided my kiss!

10:05.390 --> 10:08.690
You're the one who decides whether I kill you or die alone!

10:08.690 --> 10:11.560
I don't want to be reborn as a hopeless romantic!

10:12.230 --> 10:12.980
Sorry.

10:12.980 --> 10:16.570
I wasn't trying to avoid you, I was just a little surpri—

10:16.570 --> 10:20.150
You blockhead!

10:31.960 --> 10:33.040
Are you okay?

10:34.000 --> 10:36.420
I... like you too.

10:43.180 --> 10:44.680
Would you do me a favor?

10:45.220 --> 10:46.390
What is it?

10:46.390 --> 10:48.390
Go ahead and tell me.

10:48.390 --> 10:50.310
Please close your eyes.

10:51.100 --> 10:52.100
Why?

10:54.150 --> 10:58.740
Because even if we're on a battlefield,
you're supposed to close them.

11:00.030 --> 11:02.780
If I'm supposed to... then I guess I will.

11:12.920 --> 11:14.210
For some reason...

11:14.210 --> 11:16.670
I had a sudden feeling.

11:17.670 --> 11:21.930
That I might lose her at any moment.

11:28.510 --> 11:29.680
Saya.

11:30.930 --> 11:31.940
What is it?

11:33.650 --> 11:35.100
I just wanted to call your name.

11:37.440 --> 11:38.150
Yeah.

11:51.250 --> 11:55.830
I wonder... Why was that sword placed so conveniently near the stone statue?

11:55.830 --> 11:56.500
Huh?

11:56.500 --> 12:02.010
Don't you have this feeling like someone is toying around with us inside this labyrinth?

12:10.770 --> 12:13.390
I-It's not like I'm flustered or anything...

12:13.770 --> 12:18.860
Something like a single kiss won't throw off a professional spy.

12:18.860 --> 12:22.280
B-But that doesn't mean I'm used to it or anything.

12:22.280 --> 12:25.410
Ah... I mean that was my first kiss.

12:26.200 --> 12:27.950
It really was.

12:28.370 --> 12:30.950
In that case, isn't it fine to be excited about it?

12:37.540 --> 12:39.000
What's with that screaming?

12:39.000 --> 12:41.420
Because Riki-kun...

12:41.420 --> 12:45.300
You're looking at me like I'm overly excited.

12:45.300 --> 12:48.760
How would you feel if I told you my bottom is a <i>veteran</i> of numerous encounters?

12:48.760 --> 12:52.010
It'd be a problem if you weren't excited.

12:52.640 --> 12:53.770
Why's that?

12:53.770 --> 12:57.770
Because then you'd notice that I'm excited too.

12:58.770 --> 13:02.150
You're excited too?

13:02.150 --> 13:03.820
Of course I am.

13:04.610 --> 13:07.450
With the girl I love, for the first time—

13:10.320 --> 13:13.410
A girl really shouldn't be speaking like that...

13:13.410 --> 13:15.870
Do you really think I wanted to say "GEGEGOBO"?

13:15.870 --> 13:17.790
No one would ever say that.

13:22.130 --> 13:23.300
A-Are you okay?

13:23.300 --> 13:23.800
Listen, you!

13:23.800 --> 13:28.010
Isn't it obvious that I'd be surprised if I suddenly bumped into the person that's always on my mind?!

13:28.010 --> 13:29.640
You can understand that much, can't you?

13:29.640 --> 13:31.930
I don't understand what you're trying to imply...

13:31.930 --> 13:34.810
I'm saying that we're acting no different from a couple right now!

13:40.810 --> 13:41.480
That can't be true!

13:41.480 --> 13:45.490
No way in hell!

13:48.490 --> 13:50.570
Hey, wait...

13:50.570 --> 13:53.910
A cute girl wouldn't do that, now would she?

13:53.910 --> 13:57.910
By using a rougher way of speaking, she can cancel out the embarrassment.

13:57.910 --> 13:59.040
What the heck was that?

13:59.040 --> 14:01.500
A girl can't possibly do that to cancel out her embarrassment.

14:01.500 --> 14:02.670
<i>I can't?</i>

14:03.540 --> 14:06.170
I guess, I'm just an embarrassed girl then!

14:15.060 --> 14:17.100
Are you okay? Are you hurt anywhere?

14:19.940 --> 14:22.360
All right, that's enough screwing around.

14:27.530 --> 14:30.150
The final challenge awaits us over there.

14:30.610 --> 14:34.990
We need to get through without touching any of these...

14:38.870 --> 14:39.910
What do we do?

14:40.580 --> 14:41.960
We just have to move forward.

15:06.150 --> 15:07.940
Here we are...

15:07.940 --> 15:09.570
The final battle.

15:11.990 --> 15:17.700
Before we can reach the treasure on the final floor, we must battle him here.

15:17.700 --> 15:18.910
"Him"?

15:19.410 --> 15:21.540
The leader of the Darkness Executives.

15:21.540 --> 15:23.960
The strongest, and final boss of this world.

15:25.670 --> 15:27.500
He's waiting for us.

15:31.760 --> 15:34.930
It was as if the darkness was telling me:

15:35.510 --> 15:39.720
"If you go any further, you won't be able to meet her again."

15:41.430 --> 15:43.100
Hey, Riki-kun.

15:45.480 --> 15:48.860
What do you think the treasure at the end of this labyrinth is?

15:48.860 --> 15:49.900
Huh?

15:50.530 --> 15:55.160
Instead of riches or gold, it's said to be something revolutionary.

15:56.030 --> 15:57.620
Let's see...

15:57.620 --> 16:00.120
Maybe it's the engine of a UFO.

16:00.120 --> 16:03.160
I see, that's pretty revolutionary.

16:03.160 --> 16:05.750
The Americans and Russians would be all over it.

16:05.750 --> 16:07.750
Eh? Is that what it really is?

16:07.750 --> 16:09.630
Well, who knows?

16:10.420 --> 16:12.590
Saya, what do you think it is?

16:13.590 --> 16:17.260
I think that it's a time machine.

16:17.260 --> 16:20.060
That would be even more impressive than a UFO.

16:20.060 --> 16:23.390
I mean, if it wasn't at least something that amazing,

16:23.390 --> 16:26.690
they wouldn't be sending spies from all over the world to obtain it.

16:27.520 --> 16:29.900
A time machine, huh?

16:30.480 --> 16:34.490
If you could use that time machine, which time would you go to?

16:34.490 --> 16:36.450
Let's see...

16:36.450 --> 16:40.910
I think I'd want to look 100 years into the future, to see what it'd be like.

16:41.660 --> 16:44.120
The earth may be destroyed by then.

16:44.120 --> 16:45.920
Ah, is that so?

16:45.920 --> 16:49.880
You know, it'd be pretty stupid if you died as soon as you stepped into the future.

16:50.000 --> 16:52.630
Then, Saya, would you rather travel into the past?

16:53.300 --> 16:56.260
Yeah. If it was possible...

16:56.970 --> 16:59.180
I'd like to travel back to when I was a child.

17:01.010 --> 17:02.850
And do everything over again.

17:02.850 --> 17:07.350
I'd do it all over again, and then meet you once more.

17:16.610 --> 17:18.360
Hey, if this...

17:18.990 --> 17:19.780
Yes?

17:20.910 --> 17:21.990
If this...

17:23.580 --> 17:24.750
If...

17:28.250 --> 17:31.500
If this mission were to end successfully,

17:33.210 --> 17:34.880
would you want to go on a date together?

17:37.880 --> 17:39.890
Yeah, let's go on a date together.

17:45.390 --> 17:46.850
Well then, let's go.

17:47.140 --> 17:49.440
The mastermind awaits.

17:49.440 --> 17:50.900
Mastermind?

17:50.900 --> 17:51.860
Huh?

17:53.440 --> 17:55.690
I don't want to hear that from you.

17:56.990 --> 17:58.450
So you finally show yourself.

17:58.450 --> 17:59.570
Who's that?

17:59.570 --> 18:02.620
I am the president of the the Darkness Executives.

18:05.660 --> 18:07.830
Tokikaze Shun.

18:09.500 --> 18:13.590
I guess I should congratulate you for making it this far, huh?

18:15.880 --> 18:19.010
Oh? Look at what you've become.

18:22.510 --> 18:24.810
That's enough, Riki-kun.

18:33.980 --> 18:35.860
I have to do this alone.

18:35.860 --> 18:36.820
Alone?

18:36.820 --> 18:39.570
This is my fight.

18:39.570 --> 18:41.490
You can't do this alone!

18:42.200 --> 18:44.990
Don't worry, that's just how the rules work.

18:44.990 --> 18:48.910
We won't be able to reach the treasure if we don't follow the rules.

18:59.130 --> 18:59.970
Saya!

19:06.390 --> 19:07.260
Riki-kun.

19:09.390 --> 19:15.110
I'll take you on a date for sure, one day...

19:15.690 --> 19:17.320
Those sound like your final words.

19:18.070 --> 19:19.280
It's a promise.

19:23.350 --> 19:25.360
Here I come!

19:32.670 --> 19:34.000
You promised me...

19:38.590 --> 19:40.090
That we'd meet again...

19:42.680 --> 19:45.340
That we'd be in love,

19:45.340 --> 19:46.970
Riki-kun.

19:49.560 --> 19:50.640
And that we'd go...

19:51.810 --> 19:52.890
on a date.

19:56.060 --> 19:57.060
No matter what.

19:59.730 --> 20:01.110
Saya...

20:28.010 --> 20:29.140
I've died...

20:31.140 --> 20:33.230
I wonder how many times I've died now.

20:34.100 --> 20:35.480
Is this the 99th time?

20:37.150 --> 20:38.770
Or is it even more?

20:52.450 --> 20:55.870
And then I'll wait for Riki-kun here again.

21:07.590 --> 21:09.510
Oh, it's just the trees.

21:12.390 --> 21:14.310
What are you doing in the school building at this hour?

21:14.520 --> 21:17.520
I came to get my notebook that I left behind!

21:17.810 --> 21:22.230
Run down the hallway and leave through the front emergency exit without looking back.

21:22.570 --> 21:24.650
Start running as soon as I let go, got it?

21:25.320 --> 21:26.200
Okay, go!

21:29.950 --> 21:31.580
My Riki-kun.

21:32.160 --> 21:34.290
My one and only partner.

21:45.380 --> 21:52.130
Episode 3

21:45.380 --> 21:52.130
Darkness Executives

21:52.120 --> 21:55.300
While I ran around the bases,

21:55.600 --> 21:58.900
I suddenly stopped in my tracks

21:59.000 --> 22:05.820
To gaze at the ball that flew above my head.

22:05.480 --> 22:07.480
- Ending -

22:05.890 --> 22:09.110
I wondered why

22:09.270 --> 22:12.500
I couldn’t even get that one hit,

22:12.740 --> 22:19.060
As I stood there bewildered.

22:19.360 --> 22:26.010
One point away, yet it feels so far.

22:21.120 --> 22:24.310
To the delicate eye.

22:26.190 --> 22:29.350
Don’t you feel that way too?

22:27.900 --> 22:31.310
Even if you feel like that.

22:29.700 --> 22:38.710
I wonder if I’ll be able to stand up to bat.

22:39.730 --> 22:42.550
But I know

22:42.600 --> 22:46.640
that my story from now on

22:46.670 --> 22:54.040
Is a journey for me to become as strong as you.

22:55.980 --> 23:00.710
This scene, where various ripples, forming and expanding,

23:00.310 --> 23:03.960
Are overlapping...

23:03.560 --> 23:10.700
You must not forget, these are everyone's feelings.

23:13.400 --> 23:17.200
As I look at you sitting next to me now

23:16.980 --> 23:26.190
You seem to be a little more mature.

23:30.940 --> 23:40.940
Episode 4

23:30.940 --> 23:40.940
Sometime, somewhere...

23:32.320 --> 23:37.280
Riki-kun doesn't know anything about the treasure, or what's about to happen.

23:37.280 --> 23:40.080
And that moment of sadness is yet to come.
